2. Permitted personal use

You may, without payment or separate permission:

  a. Use an owner-operated hosted instance for personal communication with
     friends, subject to the operator granting access.
  b. Download, inspect, build, install, run and make private backup copies of
     the Software for your own personal, noncommercial use.
  c. Self-host an instance exclusively for yourself and your personal friends.
  d. Modify the Software privately for those permitted uses.
  e. Deliver the browser client assets needed by your invited friends to use
     your permitted private instance. Those friends may use and retain the
     client copies needed for that purpose, but may not redistribute them.

A private instance must be limited to invited personal friends rather than
offered to the public. Paying your own infrastructure costs does not by itself
make an otherwise permitted private instance commercial.

3. Uses requiring prior written permission

The following require prior written permission from Lovro Žeželj:

  a. Any commercial or business use, including a business using the Software
     internally, even without selling access or making a direct profit.
  b. Selling, renting, licensing or otherwise monetizing the Software or
     access to an instance, including paid hosting and advertising-supported
     services.
  c. Including the Software or portions of it in paid client deliverables or
     in products or services supplied as part of a business.
  d. Redistributing the source code, modified versions, builds, packages or
     container images, including through public forks or download mirrors,
     except for the limited browser delivery expressly allowed in section 2.
  e. Operating a publicly accessible instance for people beyond your personal
     friends, even if access is free.

Permission requests may be sent to lovro.zezelj@gmail.com. Permission must
expressly identify the use being authorized; silence is not permission.

